{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1119167-advice-on-a-storyhook","id":1119167,"title":"Advice on a storyhook","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-21T21:04:08-07:00","id":1119167,"title":"Advice on a storyhook","content":"I came up with a storyhook when Scion 2ed comes out. The basic idea is that a titanspawn of either Terra or The Drowned Road ends up releasing all the inmates in a high-security prison, causing a full scale riot. My question is which one of the titans would willingly cause a prison break and how could I get Scions to actually give a damn about the riot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T21:58:58-07:00","id":1119185,"title":"","content":"can't help you with the titans but I imagine putting sibling of the scions in the prison might work, alternately put a prophet in there who was arrested for knowing too much about a crime to not be involved, and have the prophet needed for something the scions want","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T08:55:55-07:00","id":1119257,"title":"","content":"Or, if you want a really fun introduction, you can ask your players for a list of crimes their characters might commit, no matter how ridiculous, and have them be inmates in the breakout who are trying to restore peace (maybe they were wrongly convicted by the will of the gods to make sure they were in that time and place)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T11:03:31-07:00","id":1119292,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice so far. I am wondering what kind of titanspawn would be intelligent enough to cause a mass prison riot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T11:25:05-07:00","id":1119299,"title":"","content":"Is there any reason you are looking at The Drowned Road or Terra for the source of the Titans? So far it looks like 2e has abandoned the idea of 'Greater Titans,' that 1e had. Are you looking for primarily Water / Fertility related entities? Or Theoi/Orisha ones? And, by chance, do you have any idea behind the motive for this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T11:59:08-07:00","id":1119310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1119167-advice-on-a-storyhook?p=1119299#post1119299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any reason you are looking at The Drowned Road or Terra for the source of the Titans? So far it looks like 2e has abandoned the idea of 'Greater Titans,' that 1e had. Are you looking for primarily Water / Fertility related entities? Or Theoi/Orisha ones? And, by chance, do you have any idea behind the motive for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b I considered Terra because from what I read from Greek myth, Gaia gets kinda pissy when her children gets imprisoned. Not sure if that extends to humanity or not. I don't no why I considered the Drowned Road. I also had no idea they were ditching the Greater Titans. Perhaps they are causing the prison riot to spread chaos or possibly, to recruit potential allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T13:01:44-07:00","id":1119324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1119167-advice-on-a-storyhook?p=1119310#post1119310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b I considered Terra because from what I read from Greek myth, Gaia gets kinda pissy when her children gets imprisoned. Not sure if that extends to humanity or not. I don't no why I considered the Drowned Road. I also had no idea they were ditching the Greater Titans. Perhaps they are causing the prison riot to spread chaos or possibly, to recruit potential allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humanity tends to get the shortest end of the stick in Greek mythology, the current version of humanity (Age of Iron) are unrelated to Gaia IIRC, but don't let that stop you if you're really feelin' that sort of angle to go with! There are some options I can think of here and there though. If you are specifically looking for Greek 'Titanspawn,' then I can suggest some things. Satyr are always a good option for social breakdown such as this sort of situation. In theory Gaia could have a special purpose-born creature to stir up trouble as she did with Typhon to attempt to overthrow Zeus, but that might be more of a nuclear option for her.<br /> <br /> Sometimes some of the Daimones (Personifications of forces) are credited to being her offspring, so one of them might work. Dolos is the personification of trickery and whatnot, sometimes the son of Gaia and Aether. Lyssa, the personification of violent, rage-fueled madness might work too, sometimes the daughter of Gaia and Aether. The only thing about the Daimones is they are Immortal Beings, just like the Gods themselves, so they wouldn't be totally appropriate to directly clash with some Heroes I don't think. They are probably sitting up at Legend 6-12 depending on what they are. What you could do instead is have one of these Daimones invisible (something they and the Theoi are entirely capable of doing freely), and trying to stir up trouble through a few select mortals they are guiding to lead the uprising. The players never directly confront the Daimones, just confront beings 'inspired' by them, and give the players hints that there is someone behind this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T13:53:27-07:00","id":1119335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1119167-advice-on-a-storyhook?p=1119324#post1119324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Humanity tends to get the shortest end of the stick in Greek mythology, the current version of humanity (Age of Iron) are unrelated to Gaia IIRC, but don't let that stop you if you're really feelin' that sort of angle to go with! There are some options I can think of here and there though. If you are specifically looking for Greek 'Titanspawn,' then I can suggest some things. Satyr are always a good option for social breakdown such as this sort of situation. In theory Gaia could have a special purpose-born creature to stir up trouble as she did with Typhon to attempt to overthrow Zeus, but that might be more of a nuclear option for her.<br /> <br /> Sometimes some of the Daimones (Personifications of forces) are credited to being her offspring, so one of them might work. Dolos is the personification of trickery and whatnot, sometimes the son of Gaia and Aether. Lyssa, the personification of violent, rage-fueled madness might work too, sometimes the daughter of Gaia and Aether. The only thing about the Daimones is they are Immortal Beings, just like the Gods themselves, so they wouldn't be totally appropriate to directly clash with some Heroes I don't think. They are probably sitting up at Legend 6-12 depending on what they are. What you could do instead is have one of these Daimones invisible (something they and the Theoi are entirely capable of doing freely), and trying to stir up trouble through a few select mortals they are guiding to lead the uprising. The players never directly confront the Daimones, just confront beings 'inspired' by them, and give the players hints that there is someone behind this.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat is good advice. One other possibility to why Gaia decided to send a servant to the prison is that one of her more human looking titan-spawn might've been arrested. So, she sends a second titanspawn who could easily overpower the guards in to break him or her out. But, this first titanspawn convinces the second one to break out the rest of the inmates under one of these two reasons.<br /> <br /> 1. It could give Gaia more servants.<br /> \u200b2. The first titanspawn was a satyr and he decided to release all the inmates because he thinks the anarcy and chaos it will cause will be fun.<br /> <br /> Your Daimones idea is also pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}